00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:11.308
what you're looking for to do.

00:10:11.308 --> 00:10:14.592
A couple other things that
I think are important.

00:10:14.592 --> 00:10:18.420
You need to understand the human
spirit in new technologies.

00:10:18.420 --> 00:10:21.664
In 1996, I thought that by the year 2000,

00:10:21.664 --> 00:10:25.201
every single person would come
into my dad's liquor store

00:10:25.201 --> 00:10:27.807
with a cellphone and scan the barcodes

00:10:27.807 --> 00:10:30.751
and know the price of
every wine in the country

00:10:30.751 --> 00:10:33.730
and so I'd literally lower
the price of every wine

00:10:33.730 --> 00:10:36.945
in my dad's story to cost or
the best price on the internet

00:10:36.945 --> 00:10:39.216
because what I didn't
understand was how long

00:10:39.216 --> 00:10:41.490
it would take to be accepted.

00:10:41.490 --> 00:10:45.160
Online dating was in
play for over a decade

00:10:45.160 --> 00:10:47.180
before it was culturally accepted.

00:10:47.180 --> 00:10:50.741
I think a lot of people are
making bets on singularity,

00:10:50.741 --> 00:10:54.474
on AR, on VR, on crypto, on blockchain.

00:10:54.474 --> 00:10:56.259
You understand it.

00:10:56.259 --> 00:10:58.270
You're beginning to understand it

00:10:58.270 --> 00:11:00.630
and you're making decisions
based on your belief

00:11:00.630 --> 00:11:02.760
that it will be accepted or at scale

00:11:02.760 --> 00:11:06.218
